 "title": "A record and what belongs to it",
 "caption": "It stands in a rail, the navigation and the content attached, at the body's full width: the rail is open at a desktop and shut to its icons on a tablet, and on a phone one bar stands at the top. The page level is the record: the way back, the picture of the person, the name, and the email on the line under it, with the state before it on that line: the end of the page level holds actions only. Then the lists attached to the record, each a container. A list a person adds to has a box at its top that finds a record as they type, with Add beside it, an icon on a tablet, so one is attached without leaving the page; a list that is only read has none: side by side at a desktop, two and one on a tablet, and one column on a phone. Each line ends with the action that removes it. No list shows a count.",
